DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     vveellppiicc writes the drawings named on its command line to
     standard output as ppiicc source, for figures in manuals and
     reports.  Smooth polylines come out as pic splines; layers
     marked no-print, and the construction layer, are skipped.

     The scale is PINNED at 16 grid units to the inch and there
     is no option to change it.  A figure that changed size when
     somebody passed a flag would set differently in every docu-
     ment that included it, and the point of a figure is that it
     does not.

     The file name - is standard input, so a generated drawing
     becomes a figure with no temporary file: vveelliinnffoo -ssyymmsshheeeett
     ppiidd.ssyymm | vveellppiicc - .

EEXXAAMMPPLLEESS
     A drawing per figure, in a Makefile:

                  .SUFFIXES: .d .pic
                  .d.pic: ; velpic $< > $@

SSEEEE AALLSSOO
     vveelllluumm , vveellpplloott , vveellddxxff , nnrrooffff

NNOOTTEESS
     A markup drawing from vveellddiiffff -mmaarrkk is an ordinary drawing,
     so this program draws it: the review copy on the wall and
     the figure in the manual come out of the same tool.
